ts³11100667971³1version³13³1cache_oldmajor³14³1cache_oldauthor³14³1cache_diff_default_author³11³1revision³15³1tscreate³11095175581³1text_default³1ip³2205.231.31.86³2ts³21100667971³2version³21³2name³2text_default³2data³2summary³3*³3text³3= Private Property and the Human Body =

A base axiom of <nowiki>AnCap</nowiki> talk is that you 'own' your body. This is a metaphor because the human body is significantly different from all other chattels or property and those differences disallow extending the metaphor of ownership in the ways it is with chattels or land.

The basics of ownership are control, use (or abuse), and disposal. The control and use of ones body present no problem. Disposal however does. Disposal is not only after death, but also transferral to others while alive. It is not physically possible to sell, loan, or transfer the body to someone else because the body cannot be separated from its controlling personality while that personality is still alive. Thus, not only is slavery immoral, but it is also impossible as a base concept of selling bodies. Slavery is causing the personality to use the body in certain ways under the threat of harm.

What is wanted here is the extension of the strong (once upon a time) law of private property to start its application at the human body level.

But, the application of law so that the human and body are valued less than private property is a misapplication of law and to be opposed from the start, before private property even comes into the question.





PrivatePropertyAndTheHumanBodyTalk
